<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Akusha-Dargo Union</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1844 CE (approx.) · capital Akusha</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A powerful union of self-governing Dargin communities in central Dagestan, led by the qadi of Akusha, which long resisted both khans and Russia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dargins">Dargin</a> highlands of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a> were home to free communities, called jamaats, that governed themselves without princes. By the 17th century the largest of them formed a union around the village of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akusha">Akusha</a>, whose qadi, a religious judge, served as its leading authority.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The union was a confederation of village communities with their own assemblies and customary law, coordinated by the qadi and councils of elders. It could field several thousand warriors and was among the strongest forces in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a>. Its people farmed terraced fields, herded sheep and were known for metalworking in villages such as Kubachi nearby.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleksey-yermolov">General Yermolov</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akusha">Akusha</a> forces at Levashi in 1819 and imposed Russian authority. The union was finally incorporated into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> in 1844 amid the wars of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/caucasian-imamate">Caucasian Imamate</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/akusha-dargo-union.jpg" alt="Akusha-Dargo Union" width="320" height="270"><figcaption>Image: AoifeIves &amp; Khotab · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Akusha-Dargo_Union_in_the_Late_18th_Century.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1844 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Akusha</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Dargin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Akusha-Dargo, Union of Akusha-Dargo</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1722&amp;focus=akusha-dargo-union" aria-label="Akusha-Dargo Union on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5828 674 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Akusha-Dargo Union lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6148 930L6487 457"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6487 457h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6148 930h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6148 930h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Akusha. <a href="/atlas?year=1722&amp;focus=akusha-dargo-union">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

